  "title": "Government Hidden Control Surfaces — 2026",
  "question": "What high-value government information is Freedom 250 likely missing because it lives below or between familiar entity, agency, committee and publisher layers?",
  "bluf": "Freedom 250's largest newly identified blind spot is the relationship-and-process layer between entities and final decisions. The completed program holds a 1,025-body closed-FY2025 FACA denominator, a live FY2026 agency overlay, a corrected 15-body executive-council union, a reconciled 41-center FFRDC census and a terminal 114-row control-surface census: 82 complete and 32 held through the cutoff. Waves 0–13 close the bounded research sweep, membership denominator, sparse-council stops, action joins and the complete CFTC advisory family. Wave 14 completed the governed canonical promotion at 650 Federal Group nodes, 397 institutional seed rows, 110 stable relationship endpoints, 99 typed relationships, 35 promoted membership profiles and 30 exact tree bindings, with no hierarchy-tree nodes added. A held sweep state is an evidence-routing stop and does not by itself mean that a body's legal lifecycle is inactive or terminated. A meeting, recommendation, affiliation, support relationship, board selection or approval never substitutes for later instrument, obligation, operation or effect.",
